    "notes_unique": "Battle of Guadalcanal (August 1942 - February 1943, first major Allied offensive Pacific Theatre, US Marines vs Japanese, Henderson Field airstrip, 'The Slot' naval battles, Tokyo Express, 7,100 US/31,000 Japanese dead, turning point of Pacific War, Iron Bottom Sound 50+ ships from both sides sunk, WWII relics tourism); ethnic tensions/civil war (1998-2003, 'The Tensions', Guadalcanal vs Malaitan migrants, Isatabu Freedom Movement ethnic cleansing of Malaitans, Malaita Eagle Force retaliated, government collapsed, 200+ killed, 35k+ displaced, gun culture); RAMSI (Regional Assistance Mission to Solomon Islands 2003-2017, Australian-led Pacific Islands Forum peacekeeping, restored order, rebuilt police/institutions, successful intervention, largest Pacific security operation since WWII); China switch (September 2019, switched diplomatic recognition from Taiwan to China/PRC, most significant Pacific diplomacy shift, Chinese money/infrastructure, Malaita Province refused to accept, pro-Taiwan, Sogavare centralised power); 2021 Honiara riots (November, anti-Sogavare protests, Chinatown burned, Australian troops deployed, 3 dead, China switch backlash, Malaita tensions); shell money (red-feather money from Santa Cruz, shell strings, traditional bride price, customary land transactions, parallel economy); logging (massive, Malaysian/Chinese companies, deforestation, unsustainable, corruption, 60%+ government revenue); customary land (87% communal/tribal ownership, development obstacle, disputes); Mendaña named islands 1568 (believed gold, named after King Solomon); Kennedy Island (JFK PT-109 sunk 1943, rescued by Solomon Islanders, future US president); Melanesian Brotherhood (Anglican monastic order, unique, peace missions during Tensions); East Rennell (UNESCO, largest raised coral atoll lake in world); extremely low development (one of poorest Pacific states)",
